con-leche #598's `natBigHash` (`Kernel/NatHash.lean`) is `@[extern "lean_nat_big_hash"]`, the C of
`native/nat_hash.c` (upstream's `lakefile.lean` compiles it; our `lakefile.toml` compiles no C, and the
nightly-2026-10-20 runtime does not export the symbol: every executable failed to link). Here it is
`@[implemented_by]` a Lean fold over the 64-bit words; the proofs see the same opaque function.

diff --git a/vendor/con-leche/ConLeche/Kernel/NatHash.lean b/vendor/con-leche/ConLeche/Kernel/NatHash.lean
index 8d89a9e3d9a9baf22141172260b09329bbf28b99..10c05f8928908f32d046c725a34216ca6c4c524d 100644
--- a/vendor/con-leche/ConLeche/Kernel/NatHash.lean
+++ b/vendor/con-leche/ConLeche/Kernel/NatHash.lean
@@ -51,7 +51,24 @@ replaced by `@[extern "lean_nat_hash"] opaque natHash`, see the module
 header): all 64-bit words of a big number mixed.  Only for `n ≥ 2^64`,
 which is an mpz object, as upstream's `lean_nat_big_hash` (`natHash` in
 `Kernel/Expr.lean` answers below). -/
-@[extern "lean_nat_big_hash"]
+-- con-agua patch: no `native/nat_hash.c` here (our `lakefile.toml` compiles no C, and the
+-- nightly-2026-10-20 runtime does not export `lean_nat_big_hash`): the compiled code is this Lean
+-- fold over the 64-bit words, low to high, split in halves so that it costs `O(n log n)` (a
+-- word-by-word `>>> 64` would be quadratic). Only our tools' compiled code runs it. To the
+-- proofs `natBigHash` stays an opaque function of the number.
+def natBigHashImpl (n : @& Nat) : UInt64 :=
+  go n (n.log2 / 64 + 1) 11
+where
+  /-- Mix the `k` words of `m` (`m < 2^(64 k)`) into `h`, the low half first. -/
+  go (m : Nat) (k : Nat) (h : UInt64) : UInt64 :=
+    if hk : k ≤ 1 then mixHash h (UInt64.ofNat m)
+    else
+      let lo := k / 2
+      go (m >>> (64 * lo)) (k - lo) (go (m % 2 ^ (64 * lo)) lo h)
+  termination_by k
+  decreasing_by all_goals omega
+
+@[implemented_by natBigHashImpl]
 opaque natBigHash (n : @& Nat) : UInt64
 
 end ConLeche
